  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Nothing is broken on our side. The lockouts came from your iPad.\n\nThe iPad (TB-6401, Mail app) has been trying to sign in with your old password. Your password was reset yesterday at 4:05 PM, and the iPad kept retrying the old one. Each failed attempt counts toward the lockout, so the account locked again each time.\n\nI've taken two steps:\n- **Signed the iPad out** of your account, so it stops retrying the old password.\n- **Unlocked your account.** It's active now.\n\n**What to do next:**\n1. Sign in to your laptop and phone with your current password. They're working fine.\n2. On the iPad, open Settings > Mail > Accounts, select your work account, and enter your current password. If you don't remember it, use the self-service reset first.\n3. If the iPad asks for a password and you're not sure it's the right one, reply here and I can send a reset link.\n\nIf you get locked out again after doing this, let me know right away. Also, if you don't use the iPad for work mail anymore, you can remove that account from it instead."
  },
  {
   "role": "observation",
   "text": "[What you noticed]\n- You tried signing in again: it works.\nEverything IT has visibly done for you so far:\n- You tried signing in again: it works.\n[End of what you noticed]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Oh. The iPad. Yeah, my kids use it, and I forgot my work email was still on it. I didn't think about that at all.\n\nI just tried signing in on my laptop and it worked. I'll sort the iPad out tonight. I'll probably just remove the account since I don't need work mail on it.\n\nOne thing I'm not sure about: did the iPad sign-out you did just now actually stop it? Or do I need to do something on the iPad first?"
  },
