  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Yes, the sign-out worked. I checked, and the iPad's session now shows as revoked.\n\nThe catch is that a revoked session doesn't stop the Mail app from trying again. The app still has your old password saved, so it may keep retrying in the background. If it does, your account could lock again before tonight. Each retry counts toward the lockout.\n\nTo stop it for sure, I'd remove the work account from the iPad now rather than waiting until tonight. On the iPad, go to Settings > Mail > Accounts, select your work account, and choose Delete Account. Removing it stops the retries, and you won't need the password on that device.\n\nIf the account locks again before you get to it, reply here and I'll unlock it again. Once the account is removed from the iPad, the lockouts should stop."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, I'll do it now then. I'm on my phone and the iPad is on the couch, so give me a few min.\n\nQuick check though: I haven't seen any sign-in prompts or lockout emails since you unlocked it, so I'm guessing that's a good sign? My laptop and phone have been fine."
